WEBVTT

00:00.001 --> 00:00.002
♪The Medicated Demon

00:00.001 --> 00:00.002
♪Dr. Yoshimasa Naito

00:00.001 --> 00:00.002
♪Mizonokuchi Hospital Endoscopy

00:00.001 --> 00:00.002
♪West Tokyo Division

00:00.001 --> 00:00.002
- - ♪Florsheim West
Tokyo Division Chief Officer

00:00.001 --> 00:00.002
- - ♪It's a good thing that
he brought this back too.

00:00.003 --> 00:00.004
♪Gastroenterology

00:00.003 --> 00:00.004
Note: cobagin is a spoof on cabagin

00:00.003 --> 00:00.004
♪Dr. Rikuo Shinkai

00:00.003 --> 00:00.004
♪Florsheim Monster

00:00.003 --> 00:00.004
♪General Hengel

00:00.003 --> 00:00.004
♪A Phone Call from Vamp

00:00.005 --> 00:00.006
♪Examination Room 1

00:00.005 --> 00:00.006
♪Holy Hospital of Inca

00:00.005 --> 00:00.006
♪The next day

00:00.005 --> 00:00.006
♪Samiel

00:00.005 --> 00:00.006
♪Kusatsu

00:00.005 --> 00:00.006
- - ♪You should think it an honor
to be killed at my hands, Red.

00:00.007 --> 00:00.008
♪Florsheim Monster

00:00.007 --> 00:00.008
♪Endoscopy

00:00.007 --> 00:00.008
♪Plastic Surgery

00:00.007 --> 00:00.008
♪General Hengel on the Move

00:00.007 --> 00:00.008
♪Hot Springs Manjuu Cakes

00:00.009 --> 00:01.680
♪Dumbass

00:02.760 --> 00:05.380
Go to hell, Sunred!

00:10.670 --> 00:13.059
Why the hell are you using
shampoo that smells so good?!

00:13.060 --> 00:15.280
His hair apparently
smelled better than Kayoko's.

01:51.730 --> 01:53.349
Mr. Fumi?

01:53.350 --> 01:55.380
Mr. Chikara Fumi?

01:56.560 --> 01:58.369
Is that me?

01:58.370 --> 01:59.959
You must be Mr. Fumi.

01:59.960 --> 02:00.960
Well...

02:01.560 --> 02:04.839
My name is actually Nisica.

02:04.840 --> 02:07.859
I have really bad handwriting, so whoever
was filling out my registration form

02:07.860 --> 02:10.939
must have mistook my
katakana "si" for the kanji "mi".

02:10.940 --> 02:12.749
It's actually happened before.

02:12.750 --> 02:14.749
My name is actually all katakana,

02:14.750 --> 02:17.729
so I thought it might be a
little odd to have furigana for it.

02:17.730 --> 02:19.690
Oh, I see.

02:22.780 --> 02:24.569
Please, come in.

02:24.570 --> 02:25.570
Thank you.

02:25.970 --> 02:27.080
Let's see now...

02:27.280 --> 02:30.419
An upper GI endoscopy, eh.

02:30.420 --> 02:33.499
So why do you want us to perform
an endoscopy on you, Mr. Nisica?

02:33.500 --> 02:37.479
Well, it started about three weeks ago.

02:37.480 --> 02:40.529
I started getting this tickling
sensation around my stomach.

02:40.530 --> 02:42.399
I tried taking some
over-the-counter cobagin,

02:42.400 --> 02:44.059
but it didn't help at all.

02:44.060 --> 02:46.959
I'm actually from the Incan Empire.

02:46.960 --> 02:48.289
Inca, eh?

02:48.290 --> 02:51.669
Yeah, from the boonies
of the Empire to be exact.

02:51.670 --> 02:55.899
Anyway, I went in for a check-up
at a hospital there about a week ago,

02:55.900 --> 02:58.680
and they told me I should get
myself examined as soon as possible.

02:58.960 --> 03:01.499
Did you get your blood
tested in Inca as well?

03:01.500 --> 03:04.190
Yes, I did. There was
nothing abnormal there.

03:04.870 --> 03:08.929
They also said that I
should get an endoscopy,

03:08.930 --> 03:11.319
but I couldn't get one right away
because they were overbooked.

03:11.320 --> 03:14.669
Then I had to come back
to Japan because of work.

03:14.670 --> 03:18.150
I'm assuming you're in
Kawasaki on business then?

03:19.280 --> 03:20.410
Well, yes.

03:21.390 --> 03:22.630
And what is it that you do?

03:22.890 --> 03:23.890
Pardon?

03:24.380 --> 03:25.429
For work.

03:25.430 --> 03:27.999
For work?

03:28.000 --> 03:30.499
It's actually related to... domination.

03:30.500 --> 03:31.500
I beg your pardon?

03:31.600 --> 03:34.610
Well, it's got to do
with world domination...

03:34.820 --> 03:37.399
Oh, you've got nothing to worry about.

03:37.400 --> 03:40.219
The stomach is actually
very sensitive to stress,

03:40.220 --> 03:43.909
so I was just wondering if you were
involved in some kind of a stressful job.

03:43.910 --> 03:47.079
In Inca we have a
saying that goes: "Pankt..."

03:47.080 --> 03:49.199
I'm sorry, I mean "a stomach
in pain is a mind in pain."

03:49.200 --> 03:51.710
We say the same thing in Japan as well.

03:51.900 --> 03:52.740
Oh, okay.

03:52.741 --> 03:54.209
I think I understand the problem now.

03:54.210 --> 03:56.140
Let's take a look at your stomach.

03:56.740 --> 03:59.369
Is this your first endoscopy, Mr. Nisica?

03:59.370 --> 04:00.370
It is.

04:00.510 --> 04:05.320
This medicine suppresses gastric movement
so be sure to swallow all of it Mr. Nisica.

04:05.870 --> 04:09.209
This kind of looks like rice water.

04:09.210 --> 04:11.849
And this is for numbing
the inside of your throat,

04:11.850 --> 04:15.790
so swish it around a bit in your
mouth and then swallow slowly.

04:17.400 --> 04:18.520
It tastes like strawberries.

04:21.080 --> 04:24.029
Now, rub well around the area.

04:24.030 --> 04:25.869
Have you gotten your
injection yet, Mrs. Kaneko?

04:25.870 --> 04:27.080
Not yet.

04:27.880 --> 04:30.209
My mouth is going numb.

04:30.210 --> 04:32.860
Mr. Chikara Fumi, please come in.

04:33.160 --> 04:34.910
It's actually Nisica.

04:35.800 --> 04:37.509
We're going to start the examination now.

04:37.510 --> 04:39.679
You might feel a slight pain from
getting air blown into your stomach,

04:39.680 --> 04:41.040
but please try to bear with it.

04:42.190 --> 04:44.049
Try not to cough, please.

04:44.050 --> 04:46.819
Air will escape from the stomach if
you cough, and it'll just take longer.

04:46.820 --> 04:49.579
Breathe in through your mouth,

04:49.580 --> 04:52.010
and breathe in through your nose...

04:52.160 --> 04:53.160
Just kidding.

04:53.480 --> 04:55.379
Breathe in through your mouth,

04:55.380 --> 04:57.130
and breathe out through your nose.

04:59.920 --> 05:03.070
I wonder if Nisica's done
with his check-up yet.

05:07.140 --> 05:09.349
I hope everything's okay.

05:09.350 --> 05:10.949
Nisica, Nisica!

05:10.950 --> 05:12.770
Nisica!

05:12.900 --> 05:14.339
How did it go?

05:14.340 --> 05:16.639
They said everything should be fine.

05:16.640 --> 05:18.439
Oh, thank goodness!

05:18.440 --> 05:20.909
I should be able to participate in
today's fight without any problems.

05:20.910 --> 05:24.869
All right! Let's keep the flow going and
put an end to Mr. Red once and for all!

05:24.870 --> 05:25.870
Yes, sir!

05:27.360 --> 05:31.010
Is that the best you guys can do?

05:36.330 --> 05:39.999
I'm so relieved that everything
turned out all right for you, Nisica.

05:40.000 --> 05:43.799
You had me so worried when you
mentioned that you're getting an endoscopy.

05:43.800 --> 05:45.619
I thought maybe you'd
gotten some serious disease.

05:45.620 --> 05:47.420
Were you really that worried about me?

05:47.820 --> 05:48.490
I'm flattered.

05:48.491 --> 05:50.109
There's nothing more
precious than health, they say.

05:50.110 --> 05:52.469
Pizza, pizza!

05:52.470 --> 05:56.570
Watch yourself Tiser,
you're spilling everywhere!

05:57.430 --> 05:59.679
That night, the evil
organization known as Florsheim

05:59.680 --> 06:03.820
learned and appreciated
the value of health.

06:04.370 --> 06:05.429
Mr. Fumi?

06:05.430 --> 06:07.309
Mr. Chikara Fumi?

06:07.310 --> 06:08.150
U-Um...

06:08.151 --> 06:09.389
Are you Mr. Chikara Fumi?

06:09.390 --> 06:11.480
It's actually Nisica.

06:22.760 --> 06:25.109
When can we expect
you back, General Hengel?

06:25.110 --> 06:27.029
I'll be back for dinner.

06:27.030 --> 06:30.099
What do we have planned
in terms of dinner, Samiel?

06:30.100 --> 06:33.280
I was thinking about preparing some
Korean barbecue on the hot plate.

06:33.710 --> 06:35.969
I see. In that case,

06:35.970 --> 06:40.120
I suggest you take the frozen
kalbi out of the freezer and let it thaw.

06:45.240 --> 06:48.289
Today is rather cool for a summer day,

06:48.290 --> 06:52.689
so we must also account for the possibility
that the meat will not thaw in time for dinner.

06:52.690 --> 06:55.619
To make sure, turn the
packaged meat upside down

06:55.620 --> 06:58.699
and have it face the stainless
steel surface near the sink.

06:58.700 --> 06:59.070
Yes, sir.

06:59.670 --> 07:01.029
But General,

07:01.030 --> 07:04.019
we currently only have one
pack of kalbi in the freezer.

07:04.020 --> 07:05.419
Only one pack, you say?

07:05.420 --> 07:09.589
That's not remotely enough to
feed everyone, wouldn't you say?

07:09.590 --> 07:11.179
Don't tell me...

07:11.180 --> 07:14.019
Were you planning on throwing
some sausages on the grill afterwards

07:14.020 --> 07:17.030
and calling that Korean barbecue?

07:18.450 --> 07:19.789
No, sir.

07:19.790 --> 07:21.829
We actually also have
some pork fillet blocks,

07:21.830 --> 07:24.969
which can be used right away
as they have not been frozen.

07:24.970 --> 07:28.149
I was thinking that we should cut those into
large pieces and grill them with the kalbi.

07:28.150 --> 07:29.979
Pork fillets, you say?

07:29.980 --> 07:32.499
What do you think, General?

07:32.500 --> 07:34.709
All right, this is what we're going to do.

07:34.710 --> 07:37.920
Today's Korean barbecue is cancelled.

07:39.020 --> 07:41.639
We'll have fillet cutlets
for dinner instead.

07:41.640 --> 07:43.439
Pork fillet doesn't have too much fat,

07:43.440 --> 07:46.699
so it's not as delicious
when it's grilled and crispy.

07:46.700 --> 07:49.479
There's no need to
force it on to the grill.

07:49.480 --> 07:53.039
More importantly, given the
fact that pork goes bad quickly,

07:53.040 --> 07:57.179
it is wise to use it first especially
if it has not yet been frozen.

07:57.180 --> 08:00.149
You were so taken by the
idea of making Korean barbecue,

08:00.150 --> 08:03.789
that you had completely forgotten to examine
this from the fillet's point of view.

08:03.790 --> 08:07.359
Thus tonight's menu is now
effectively changed to fillet cutlets.

08:07.360 --> 08:08.970
Understood.

08:09.370 --> 08:11.369
I must have lost track of time.

08:11.370 --> 08:12.940
I should get going.

08:13.340 --> 08:16.739
But General, you really don't
have to bother yourself by going,

08:16.740 --> 08:18.039
I can always go instead.

08:18.040 --> 08:19.099
No.

08:19.100 --> 08:22.640
I must make amends for my mistakes.

08:23.240 --> 08:26.079
It is my fault for mistakenly taking
Vamp's share of the souvenirs

08:26.080 --> 08:30.629
at the monthly meeting
in Kusatsu yesterday.

08:30.630 --> 08:32.739
But didn't Master Vamp say over the phone

08:32.740 --> 08:36.309
that it is okay for you
to eat his share as well?

08:36.310 --> 08:40.339
Do you really think that merits
me eating his share as well mine?

08:40.340 --> 08:42.939
It was I who mistakenly
took his Manju cakes after all.

08:42.940 --> 08:44.070
O-Of course not, sir.

08:44.670 --> 08:47.039
I'm off then. Take care
of things while I'm gone.

08:47.040 --> 08:48.040
Yes, sir!

09:00.230 --> 09:01.530
Hey there, big boy.

09:09.070 --> 09:10.240
I've arrived.

09:24.530 --> 09:25.970
Are they not home?

09:26.630 --> 09:30.929
I had hoped that at least someone
would be home in case Vamp wasn't,

09:30.930 --> 09:35.220
but I guess it would have been
wiser to call them beforehand.

09:35.400 --> 09:36.330
Should I come back later?

09:36.331 --> 09:38.749
No, even as I speak,

09:38.750 --> 09:42.229
the Manju cakes' soft crusts
are probably hardening.

09:42.230 --> 09:44.890
I've not a moment to lose.

09:46.250 --> 09:47.470
That rules this out.

09:48.880 --> 09:51.509
Their laundry is still out to dry,

09:51.510 --> 09:53.810
while the bicycle is still parked outside.

10:03.070 --> 10:04.649
Oh, Vamp.

10:04.650 --> 10:07.409
What a pity I couldn't see you today.

10:07.410 --> 10:11.090
Did you see the Manju cakes
I left in the bicycle's basket?

10:11.580 --> 10:14.019
Seeing that your laundry was still hanging

10:14.020 --> 10:15.979
despite it being a cloudy day,

10:15.980 --> 10:18.759
I judged that you hadn't gone far

10:18.760 --> 10:23.000
and figured it would be safe
to leave them inside the bicycle.

10:23.140 --> 10:26.489
Thank you so much for coming
over all the way from Tokyo.

10:26.490 --> 10:29.860
Ah yes, we were at a fight.

10:29.910 --> 10:30.949
That's right.

10:30.950 --> 10:32.599
I'll make sure you get your umbrella back.

10:32.600 --> 10:35.200
Yes, sir. Have a good day, sir.

10:36.090 --> 10:39.010
Was that Master Vamp, sir?

10:39.070 --> 10:43.829
Yes, it seems that they came back soon
after I left, just as I thought they would.

10:43.830 --> 10:44.830
I see.

10:46.300 --> 10:51.149
That's right. Those Manju cakes
must have been a godsend for them.

10:51.150 --> 10:54.400
It's a good thing I brought them over.

10:54.940 --> 10:57.020
Hey there, big boy.

11:02.610 --> 11:05.399
Yeah, it's pretty useful isn't it?

11:05.400 --> 11:09.130
Plus it's got a lid so it's perfect for
take-out from beef bowl restaurants.

11:09.150 --> 11:13.039
I wonder what Kayoko
could possibly be talking about

11:13.040 --> 11:15.321
with an evil guy who's
scheming on taking over the world.

11:26.960 --> 11:29.850
Maybe I should make it shorter.
